# Onboard parameters for Vehicle 1
#
# STAGE 6 - FLEET POLICY: RadioMaster transmitter -- stick order and channel
# calibration. Independent of vision, UART and the container. Loads on every FC.
#
# Read off drone 20's FC on 2026-11-01 after QGC's Radio calibration with the fleet's
# RadioMaster (px4/params/fleet/drone20-radiomaster-2026-11-01.params). Every drone
# flies with the same transmitter model and the same model setup, so the endpoints,
# trims and deadzones are the same on every FC; the per-transmitter spread is a few
# microseconds inside the 10 us deadzone.
#
# RC_MAP_ROLL/PITCH/THROTTLE/YAW = 1/2/3/4   AETR. The May-07 reference dump (and so
#                      00_baseline.params until 2026-11-01) carried TAER (4/3/2/1) from a
#                      different model setup: flashing that onto a RadioMaster drone
#                      scrambles the sticks. Arm (7), kill (5) and flight mode (6) are in
#                      05 / the baseline.
# RC1..RC4             sticks: 982 / 1494 / 2005, deadzone 10; throttle (RC3) trims at
#                      its minimum, 982, which is what PX4 expects for a non-centring
#                      throttle.
# RC5..RC8             switches: 1000 / 1500 / 2000, deadzone 10.
# RC9..RC18            unused, PX4 defaults, pinned here so the baseline carries no RC<n>_*
#                      rows at all (one place defines the radio).
#
# Fleet-wide, not per-unit, since 2026-11-01: tools/param_diff.py and
# ~/pixhawk_autoparams.py no longer treat RC<n>_(MIN|MAX|TRIM|DZ|REV) as calibration.
# Kept out of 00_baseline.params so --make-baseline still reproduces the baseline from
# the May-07 dump. A drone with a different transmitter needs its own file instead of
# this one. Reboot the FC after loading.
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	RC_MAP_ROLL	1	6
1	1	RC_MAP_PITCH	2	6
1	1	RC_MAP_THROTTLE	3	6
1	1	RC_MAP_YAW	4	6
1	1	RC1_MIN	982.000000	9
1	1	RC1_TRIM	1494.000000	9
1	1	RC1_MAX	2005.000000	9
1	1	RC1_DZ	10.000000	9
1	1	RC1_REV	1.000000	9
